  "sport": "soccer",
  "title": "Wall pass in the lane",
  "description": "Mark out a lane about 25 × 15 metres with a line at each end and a cone in the middle as a pretend defender. A wall player stands on each side of the cone. A dribbles straight at the cone, plays a one-two and gets the ball back behind the cone. A then passes to E at the far end and joins that line. E does the same coming back, using the wall on the other side. Swap the wall players after a while.\n\nProgression: replace the cone with a defender who is half-active at first and later allowed to win the ball. With lots of players, run two lanes side by side.\n\nVariant for more touches: in a 30 × 20 metre box, two ball carriers, three wall players and three defenders move freely. The ball carriers look for a defender to take on and a wall player to combine with. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Dribble straight at the defender so they think you will go past."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Pass to the wall at the right distance – not too early, not too late."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "The wall stands half-turned and plays it first time in front of the runner."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Speed up straight after the pass and run past on the other side."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
